Jean Hayworth was lying in a pool of blood on the floor of her son's nursery. Tight in her arms was her baby boy. He didn't stir. His face was blotchy and red and blood caked his sleeper suit and the back of his head. It was clear Billy Jean was deceased. To Roy's relief, her baby was still breathing. All of the blood around him belonged to his mother. The baby himself was unhurt. Linda broke down as she described the condition of the little boy to the 911 operator. Quote, The baby kind of to me as a parent looks like maybe it's been crying for a while and probably cried till he can't cry no more. Both Bill and Billy Jean had been shot in the head. There were also deep slash wounds across Bill's neck, although it was unclear
正躺在她儿子婴儿房地板的一滩血泊中。她紧紧怀抱着自己的小男孩。他一动不动。他的脸红一块白一块，血迹沾满了他的连体睡衣和后脑勺。显然，比利·琼已经死亡。令罗伊宽慰的是，她的宝宝还在呼吸。他身边的所有鲜血都属于他的母亲。婴儿本身没有受伤。琳达在向 911 接线员描述小男孩的情况时情绪崩溃了。原话是：“作为一名家长，在我看来这个宝宝好像已经哭了很久，可能哭到再也哭不出来为止。”比尔和比利·琼的头部都中了枪。比尔的脖子上也有深深的刀伤，尽管目前尚不清楚

